  "prefLabel": "Ret 304.10 Notice of Service Adjustment",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-10-10",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ret 304.10 Notice of Service Adjustment. After discovery, through an audit or other means, of service credit being incorrectly granted or denied a member pursuant to RSA 100-A:4, the NHRS shall issue to the member or beneficiary and employer a notice of service adjustment which sets forth the:\n\n(a) Name of member or beneficiary;\n\n(b) The last four digits of the member or beneficiary’s Social Security number;\n\n(c) Name of employer;\n\n(d) Time period of service which was incorrectly granted or denied a member;\n\n(e) Amount of service credit which was incorrectly granted or denied a member; and\n\n(f) Member’s total corrected amount of service credit.\n\nSource. #7478, eff 4-10-01; ss by #7573, eff 10-10-01, EXPIRED: 10-10-09\n\nNew. #9562, eff 10-14-09; ss by #10111, eff 4-11-12; ss by #12707, eff 1-9-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ret100-500.html"
